# Shared by both frontend/Dockerfile and backend/Dockerfile — both build from the repo root
# context. backend/Dockerfile needs .git/ present so MinVer can resolve the release version at
# publish time (see backend/Directory.Build.props), so it is NOT excluded here. Modern BuildKit
# only transfers paths actually COPY'd by whichever Dockerfile is building, so listing both
# sides' excludes together doesn't slow either build down.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/logs/
**/uploads/
**/coverage/
.serena/
.codegraph/
# agent tooling — .claude/worktrees/ and .worktrees/ hold whole repo checkouts (with their own
# .env*/node_modules), which must never ride along in the build context.
.claude/
.worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/
plans/
monitoring/
**/*.md
**/tests/

# Real secrets — never bake into any image, only the *.Example.json / *.example files are templates.
# Every pattern here is anchored to the build-context root (the repo root), so a bare
# `appsettings.json` would only match a file at the repo root — the `**/` prefix is what actually
# reaches backend/src/StarterKit.API/appsettings.json and frontend/.env*.
**/appsettings*.json
!**/appsettings*.Example.json

.vs/
*.user

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
